1
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:42,820
Something will work out, I'm sure.

2
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without work, come to me.

3
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,480
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

4
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:18,220
Look, even the burning steel
will somehow be fine eventually.

5
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:27,460
You understand, right? Got it, got it.
Once you do, gather up and follow me.

6
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:42,960
Fly! Flying Squadron!

7
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,100
The loan's open?

8
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:17,220
I'm sure I closed it when I left.

9
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:28,280
Targeting an apartment less than
five minutes from our police box

10
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:30,800
They're completely looking down on us,
aren't they?

11
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:33,520
That's the place

12
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:42,260
Go ahead. Thanks for your hard work.
How's things down there?

13
00:02:42,810 --> 00:02:45,380
So far,
nothing has turned up besides the victim.

14
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:59,260
What a mess they made. The losses are about 50,000 yen in cash,
two bags from a famous luxury brand, and

15
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:00,380
accessories worth 500,000 yen.

16
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:01,740
And the victim is

17
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:05,660
downstairs being questioned
while we examine the scene.

18
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:07,720
There they are.

19
00:03:07,720 --> 00:03:10,440
So you did lock the door properly?

20
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:13,040
Yes, I used the double lock.

21
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:15,840
There were security alarms
on the windows too, right?

22
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:18,260
Yes, I had them on every window.

23
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:22,180
I even had the latest
model on the front door lock.

24
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:26,440
But if the front door was unlocked,

25
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:28,700
then it was a picking burglar after all?

26
00:03:29,260 --> 00:03:30,820
Couldn't it have been
opened from the inside?

27
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:33,140
From the inside?

28
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,420
They got in from over there,
from the side of the street.

29
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:42,020
No way, it was the sixth floor.

30
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:44,500
Ryotsu, stop talking nonsense!

31
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:46,380
That's impossible!

32
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:48,940
I can do it. Just watch.

33
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:52,120
W-what are you doing?

34
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:56,380
Amazing.

35
00:03:57,700 --> 00:04:01,100
How did they manage to jump up that high?

36
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:03,340
Come on, you can do it, right?

37
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:05,760
But up to the sixth floor...

38
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:06,860
It's easy.

39
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:10,060
What do you think you're doing?

40
00:04:10,060 --> 00:04:14,160
That's how you climb up, you see.

41
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:15,440
Incredible.

42
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:17,900
He really started climbing.

43
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:19,840
Wow, that's impressive.

44
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:28,840
Chief, we've reached the sixth floor.
We're going into the room now.

45
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:31,060
What a guy.

46
00:04:31,660 --> 00:04:36,800
The balcony window is locked
and has a burglar alarm on it, so

47
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:38,980
It was probably through the bathroom.

48
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,280
Sure enough,
there are signs it was forced open.

49
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:47,480
He's taking the bathroom window off.

50
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:47,960
What?

51
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:52,640
Guess this much is enough to get through.

52
00:04:54,860 --> 00:04:55,820
He went in.

53
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:57,640
What's with that guy?

54
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:59,140
He just went right in.

55
00:04:59,580 --> 00:05:01,340
Only one minute after climbing up.

56
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:02,980
That's incredible speed.

57
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:07,240
Take the glass out and
the window stays shut.

58
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:08,560
So,

59
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:11,480
the security buzzer definitely won't go off.

60
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:14,260
It's a method on par with a pro's.

61
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:15,820
See, I did it, didn't I?

62
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:18,100
Senpai.

63
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,660
You only just went inside a moment ago.

64
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:22,560
Why are you here?

65
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:25,500
I took the elevator down,

66
00:05:26,050 --> 00:05:27,560
went through the auto-lock at the entrance,

67
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:29,460
and walked right out in plain sight.

68
00:05:33,260 --> 00:05:34,860
You're the culprit, aren't you?

69
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,460
Don't be ridiculous.

70
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:38,700
Shut up.

71
00:05:41,020 --> 00:05:44,040
Why do you always carry a
multi-purpose screwdriver?

72
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:45,900
That's a key chain.

73
00:05:46,340 --> 00:05:48,560
Nakagawa, check if he has anything else.

74
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:49,080
Yes.

75
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:50,140
W-what?

76
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:52,700
Stop it, let go!

77
00:05:54,380 --> 00:06:07,380
A multi-purpose screwdriver, a mini flashlight, lock picks, even a knife!
Aren't they all burglary tools? No, they're for survival! Hey, come down to the station with me for a bit.

78
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:16,980
Hey, stop being an idiot, it'd be quicker to just say so!
Chief, if I were a thief, I wouldn't target a student's room like this.

79
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:20,900
Without hesitation, Nakagawa,
I'd go for Reiko's apartment building.

80
00:06:21,900 --> 00:06:23,820
Well, when you put it that way,
you're right.

81
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:26,420
If you have thieves' earnings...

82
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:30,920
Why do I have to eat nothing but convenience
store rice balls for a whole month?

83
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:32,460
You're as bad as him.

84
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:36,720
For a student, living alone in an
apartment like this is not allowed!

85
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,760
Even if you say that...

86
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:42,800
My dad and mom said it's safe because
it's an auto-lock apartment, so...

87
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,080
That overconfidence is dangerous, you know.

88
00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:48,600
R-really?

89
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:52,680
Precisely because it's an auto-lock
apartment that's hard to get into,

90
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:57,180
once someone's inside, everyone assumes
they're a resident and doesn't suspect a thing.

91
00:06:57,660 --> 00:07:00,960
Once inside,
you can take the elevator to any floor.

92
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:03,820
Just because it's a high
floor doesn't mean you're safe.

93
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:10,380
In the morning, when people take out the garbage or drop off their kids,
they often forget to lock up.

94
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:14,060
Burglars often target that brief moment.

95
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:17,300
A pro can steal in just two minutes.

96
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:19,360
That's awfully detailed, isn't it?

97
00:07:20,620 --> 00:07:23,120
Should we just bring him
to the station after all?

98
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:24,740
I already told you, it's not me.

99
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:27,700
Knows that much and has the
ability to pull it off too.

100
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:29,240
It's only natural that you'd be suspected.

101
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,260
I'm telling you, it's not me.

102
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:33,980
Anyway, these burglars blend
right in with the residents.

103
00:07:33,980 --> 00:07:36,040
They're often right nearby.

104
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:39,620
That cop sure knows a lot.

105
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:41,080
His skills are impressive too.

106
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:44,460
Hey, he climbed up here
and got in in one minute.

107
00:07:44,460 --> 00:07:46,900
Even I'd need three minutes, what is this?

108
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:49,060
Think he'd target elderly folks at the bank?

109
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:51,020
That'd be easier

110
00:07:51,020 --> 00:07:53,860
If I were you,
I'd target the elderly at the bank.

111
00:07:53,860 --> 00:07:55,480
Why?

112
00:07:55,600 --> 00:08:00,200
They carry lots of cash and are easy to fool,
so the success rate is high too.

113
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:03,640
He thinks just like us.

114
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:06,040
Isn't he one of them?

115
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:07,500
Hey?

116
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:10,660
W-what is it, Officer?

117
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:12,380
What kind of prediction is this?

118
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:15,640
There's no way the No. 3
"Queen" is coming in.

119
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:19,700
For this race, it's the 4, 8, and 14.
That's the lock.

120
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:22,600
Buy a trifecta box. Got it?

121
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:23,020
Yes.

122
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:27,060
If it hits,
bring me a treat up on the bridge up ahead.

123
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:28,060
See ya.

124
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:29,140
Thanks.

125
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:31,260
What kind of cop is he?

126
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:33,520
Staying here is bad for my heart.

127
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:34,900
Let's find another spot.

128
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:40,720
The red dots mark wanted suspect No. 707.

129
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:45,540
The blue dots are the scenes where wanted suspect No.
745 broke in.

130
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:48,600
They were centered around
Adachi and Edogawa wards.

131
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:52,900
Looks like two groups of criminals
have invaded Katsushika Ward.

132
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:56,060
So they're increasing
the number of patrol cars

133
00:08:56,060 --> 00:08:58,280
and beefing up patrols.

134
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:00,600
Micro-level moves like that won't work.

135
00:09:01,020 --> 00:09:02,080
Ryotsu

136
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,220
Even if we add more patrol cars,

137
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:08,100
there's only so much we can do to
thoroughly patrol all of Katsushika Ward.

138
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:10,260
That's true, but

139
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:13,772
it'll also put pressure on the criminals,

140
00:09:13,822 --> 00:09:16,840
and there's no other way to stop the damage.

141
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:21,080
There is. We keep watch from the sky.

142
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:25,340
From the sky? You mean use a helicopter?

143
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:28,701
A helicopter's too fast,

144
00:09:28,751 --> 00:09:33,660
and with that huge propeller noise, the criminals would notice right away.
It'd backfire.

145
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:36,340
If not a helicopter, then a plane?

146
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:45,100
Isn't there a vehicle that flies slowly
enough to intimidate the criminals?

147
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:49,920
Just leave it to me.

148
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:01,040
Right, this is our chance.

149
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:10,620
Yeah, leave some cash behind so they
don't realize it was a burglary right away.

150
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:11,060
Yeah.

151
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:15,680
The residents will be back soon,
so let's escape through the balcony.

152
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:18,520
Okay, nobody's here.

153
00:10:32,060 --> 00:10:34,380
Alright, this place is fine too.

154
00:10:38,820 --> 00:10:41,760
This is eco-friendly, and it's quiet too,

155
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:45,780
so we can keep watch on the
ground by flying low and slow.

156
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:48,880
I never imagined an airship would work.

157
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:52,800
You can really see each room in the apartment buildings,
can't you?

158
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:56,000
Since it's slow,
we can check every corner thoroughly.

159
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:58,700
What's with those two?

160
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:00,380
They're suspicious.

161
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:02,220
Lower the rope!

162
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:03,820
What's that?

163
00:11:03,820 --> 00:11:05,460
They're coming down.

164
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:08,260
Those guys are too much!

165
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,380
Nakagawa, alert Shon!

166
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:10,780
Yes!

167
00:11:11,060 --> 00:11:13,060
Katsushika Station, we're in trouble! Run!

168
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:17,220
If we wait for the patrol car,
they'll get away!

169
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:19,800
I'll catch them myself!

170
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:25,880
Senpai!

171
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:26,640
Ryotsu!

172
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:27,640
He jumped!

173
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:31,860
Y-you idiot!

174
00:11:32,020 --> 00:11:32,660
We did it!

175
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:35,900
Yes!

176
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:37,620
W-what!

177
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:38,980
Hey!

178
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:42,500
You two are the ones from the other day...

179
00:11:44,060 --> 00:11:45,720
Please analyze the results.

180
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:48,020
Alright, pull back.

181
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:56,660
W-what?

182
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:59,460
Wanted suspect No. 707?

183
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:01,500
We hit the jackpot, Chief!

184
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:04,680
I'm sending you the suspect's photo now.

185
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:08,980
This is the wanted photo of No. 707.

186
00:12:08,980 --> 00:12:11,840
Yeah, it's coming through to my phone now.

187
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:18,760
Really? Good work, Ohara.

188
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:19,780
Thank you very much.

189
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:32,880
I have to hand it to you,
patrolling by airship!

190
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:39,680
Well, I've been insisting for a long time that airship patrols
are absolutely necessary,

191
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:42,880
and it just so happened that the
higher-ups finally approved it.

192
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:47,700
It's all thanks to the higher-ups
for making such a brilliant decision.

193
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:51,780
No, no. It was only because the
Chief used his authority to order it.

194
00:12:51,780 --> 00:12:55,640
It was only because of Ohara's advice.

195
00:12:58,500 --> 00:13:00,640
You're really something, you know that?

196
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:03,780
It was my idea, and you went and
stole all the credit, you bastard!

197
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:04,480
Excuse me.

198
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:08,020
Well, here's my card.

199
00:13:09,140 --> 00:13:10,920
You're the photographer.

200
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:14,080
This was really Ryo-san's idea, wasn't it?

201
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:14,600
Yeah.

202
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:18,040
For a superior to take credit
for a subordinate's achievement...

203
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:19,260
That's really awful.

204
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:20,460
Right?

205
00:13:20,460 --> 00:13:22,960
You're a pretty good guy, you know.

206
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:23,700
Thank you very much.

207
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:27,960
Our magazine will definitely
feature Ryo-san too.

208
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:29,520
Please let me take your picture.

209
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:30,380
Yeah.

210
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:36,360
I like you even more now.

211
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:37,800
Thanks.

212
00:13:38,220 --> 00:13:38,940
Speaking of which,

213
00:13:40,920 --> 00:13:48,180
I'd also like to take photos from the airship, but could I ride along too?
Well, since it'll be flying every day from now on, just let me know anytime...

214
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:49,600
Thank you.

215
00:13:54,580 --> 00:14:04,600
Ryo-san, isn't Odaiba outside our jurisdiction? It's a special bonus!
The location's better than any qualifications, so it's worth the shot, right?

216
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:05,760
Hey!

217
00:14:07,780 --> 00:14:08,940
What's wrong?

218
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:13,060
On that boat, rock singer Joe Miyake
and actress Momoko Matsushita are...

219
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:13,400
What?

220
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:16,540
It's a scoop!
Please lower the altitude a little more.

221
00:14:16,540 --> 00:14:16,920
Right.

222
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:23,560
It's a huge scoop. Thank you so much.

223
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:27,000
This isn't much,
but it's for the coverage expenses.

224
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:30,520
Right. I'll pass it along to
the public relations department.

225
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:32,300
Well, excuse me.

226
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:36,820
Is this the coverage budget?

227
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:42,840
This much?

228
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:43,960
Wow, this is...

229
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:51,880
We're about to reach the destination.

230
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:53,300
Alright, here we go!

231
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:02,620
As expected of the home of the
top-selling actor in the film world!

232
00:15:02,620 --> 00:15:03,560
It's too huge.

233
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:07,460
That actor famous for playing
serious ground-level roles...

234
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:08,860
in broad daylight...

235
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:10,000
Okay!

236
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,700
Alright, everyone, let's go!

237
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:19,800
What's that? There's someone over there.

238
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:20,980
What are they doing?

239
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:22,320
Which one?

240
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:23,420
Where?

241
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:26,000
That apartment next to the mansion.

242
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,200
Whoa! That's - !

243
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:34,440
Volvo! Bring me the 745 wanted poster!

244
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:39,900
Yeah! It's the 745 wanted poster!

245
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:44,060
Yes! No doubt about it! Volvo!
Get us close to that apartment!

246
00:15:44,300 --> 00:15:45,080
Let's catch them!

247
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:46,180
Roger!

248
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:48,880
Mine!

249
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:57,320
Ryotsu, we've now received complaints
from six of Joe Miyake's offices

250
00:15:57,320 --> 00:15:59,760
by phone and email!

251
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:02,160
You took a weekly magazine
photographer up in the airship

252
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:04,780
and let him take pictures like this,
did you not?

253
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:07,500
I have no idea what you're talking about.

254
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:08,540
Don't lie!

255
00:16:08,660 --> 00:16:11,820
According to the offices, the only airship
that could get photos from this angle

256
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:14,920
was this one. That's what they're saying!

257
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:17,740
At this rate, for lack of supervision,

258
00:16:17,740 --> 00:16:19,800
our heads could come flying off!

259
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:23,740
Now, don't get so worked up about it.

260
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:27,840
Thanks to that, we were able to arrest wanted suspect No.
745, after all.

261
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:28,940
W-what?

262
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:31,260
Okay, bring him in.

263
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:37,660
There's no doubt, it's No. 745.

264
00:16:39,840 --> 00:16:40,720
It's true.

265
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:46,020
The chief has now arrested a wanted criminal that
neither the chief nor headquarters could catch.

266
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:48,560
Two of them, no less. He's quite the chief.

267
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,290
At this rate, he'll end up a top
executive at headquarters, or rather,

268
00:16:51,340 --> 00:16:54,140
Commissioner General isn't
out of the question, is it?

269
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:57,740
C-Commissioner General?

270
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:10,580
If that happens, couldn't the
Chief become the head of our station?

271
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:12,700
S-station head?

272
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:15,620
S-station...

273
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:26,400
Even so, is there still something

274
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:31,900
Well, we'll take care of things on this end.

275
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:36,100
Ryotsu, keep up the good work as
captain of the flying squadron.

276
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:36,940
Yes.

277
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:47,660
I never imagined that just
painting a logo and flying around

278
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:50,140
would bring in this much money.

279
00:17:51,060 --> 00:17:54,300
But isn't making money
off the airship a bad idea?

280
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:57,540
This is purely a side benefit of the patrol.

281
00:17:57,540 --> 00:18:00,560
Just flying around intimidates the criminals

282
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:03,980
and prevents crimes before they happen,
so you can't complain.

283
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:05,360
Well, I suppose so.

284
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:10,360
Yes, this is Ryotsu.
Money-Ringing Electric Light?

285
00:18:11,060 --> 00:18:12,580
Money-Ringing Electric Light?

286
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,960
Ronny's rival company, right?

287
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:17,584
Yeah, yeah, I see.

288
00:18:17,634 --> 00:18:21,370
Your budget is 5 million yen,
is that all right? Yes,

289
00:18:21,420 --> 00:18:22,480
Understood.

290
00:18:23,100 --> 00:18:25,480
Rejoice!
More advertising money is coming in!

291
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:27,500
Haha, w-wow, that's amazing.

292
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:31,020
Yes! Hey, are you with Toyoyama Motors?

293
00:18:31,460 --> 00:18:37,680
Well, well, Toyoyama Motors! I see,
it's the Hamasaki Hikaru new song campaign?

294
00:18:38,840 --> 00:18:45,740
Senpai, this isn't a flying billboard anymore!
On top of that, there's writing where you can't even see it from below.

295
00:18:46,300 --> 00:18:57,620
As long as it's written somewhere, that's all that matters! Besides, look at all these company names and ads.
It shows the sluggish Japanese economy can still hold its own!

296
00:18:58,140 --> 00:19:02,240
But isn't it bad that the Katsushika
Police Station name isn't anywhere?

297
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:05,700
Don't worry, it's still there.

298
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:07,520
Senpai, where?

299
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,400
More to the left.

300
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:11,280
Nowhere.

301
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:12,620
There it is!

302
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:16,640
Senpai, it's way too small.

303
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:21,080
Shouldn't it at least be as
big as the Heart Bus Tour one?

304
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:23,860
It's fine as long as it's written.

305
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:26,600
Heart Bus Tour.

306
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:30,900
That's it!
I've got a way to make even more money!

307
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:41,200
What do you mean, not a single customer?

308
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:42,020
Well, then.

309
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:52,700
Who'd have thought we could
sightsee over Tokyo from the sky?

310
00:19:53,140 --> 00:19:56,780
And we get to watch a
soccer match for free, too!

311
00:19:57,620 --> 00:19:59,780
Good thing we cancelled that bus tour.

312
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:04,380
Who'd have guessed you'd poach
the bus tour customers like that?

313
00:20:04,380 --> 00:20:08,240
You really are a genius when
it comes to business, senpai.

314
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:13,160
Don't they sell boxed lunches
or juice on this airship?

315
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:16,080
Sorry, but we don't
offer that kind of service.

316
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:17,600
Boxed lunches.

317
00:20:18,380 --> 00:20:21,980
That's it! I've thought of
a way to make even more money!

318
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:27,740
Only one passenger showed up today.

319
00:20:27,740 --> 00:20:29,520
It's pretty much the same for us.

320
00:20:29,520 --> 00:20:31,840
Everyone's cancelling on us lately.

321
00:20:32,700 --> 00:20:34,380
What on earth has gotten into them?

322
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:42,800
Sorry to keep you waiting after so long.

323
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:46,560
Would you like some airship
merchandise as a souvenir of your flight?

324
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:51,880
Airship specialty,
airship juice, airship specialty.

325
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:55,080
We also have picture books,
T-shirts, and lots more.

326
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:01,600
Senpai, table three ordered
three more servings of yakitori.

327
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:05,300
Right, this one's for table seven.
Plate it up.

328
00:21:05,300 --> 00:21:05,980
Yes.

329
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,560
Business is booming, isn't it?

330
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:12,460
I never expected it to
be this much of a hit.

331
00:21:12,460 --> 00:21:16,460
Two million per flight, and if it flies
three times a day, that's six million.

332
00:21:16,460 --> 00:21:18,020
If we keep it up for a month,

333
00:21:18,020 --> 00:21:21,000
that's 180 million yen!

334
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:24,520
Even after subtracting materials and upkeep,
that's still a hundred million in profit

335
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:26,500
Maybe we should make this our main business,

336
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:28,820
and make the police work our side job

337
00:21:32,280 --> 00:21:34,040
I went to headquarters today,

338
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:39,200
and regarding the arrests of wanted suspects No.
707 and No. 745,

339
00:21:39,200 --> 00:21:42,560
the Superintendent General
gave me words of praise.

340
00:21:43,180 --> 00:21:44,660
That's wonderful news.

341
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:49,000
As for the promotions
Ryotsu mentioned for us,

342
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,080
maybe they're not just a dream after all.

343
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:52,920
Indeed.

344
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:57,280
Chief, shall we invite Ryotsu
out for a drink tonight?

345
00:21:57,280 --> 00:21:58,040
Sounds good.

346
00:21:58,040 --> 00:22:01,460
It's about time he came back from patrol.

347
00:22:01,460 --> 00:22:02,740
I'll give him a call.

348
00:22:08,180 --> 00:22:08,980
Oh no!

349
00:22:08,980 --> 00:22:12,320
Honda, bring that fire
extinguisher over here!

350
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:13,100
Yes!

351
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:15,480
It's cramped in here!

352
00:22:16,020 --> 00:22:16,860
Okay, here goes!

353
00:22:19,320 --> 00:22:20,720
It's not coming out!

354
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:23,020
This is the ignition key!

355
00:22:23,420 --> 00:22:24,380
What?!

356
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:27,840
Oh no, the money!

357
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:31,320
Don't worry! It'll go out right away!

358
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:33,000
Use this to put it out!

359
00:22:34,860 --> 00:22:36,220
The fire's spreading!

360
00:22:41,620 --> 00:22:44,460
The sunset is unusually red today, isn't it?

361
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:48,640
Yeah, well, the sun, I mean -

362
00:22:48,690 --> 00:22:52,280
A fireball is heading this way!

363
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:53,643
That's...

364
00:22:53,693 --> 00:22:56,520
No way, it's the airship!

365
00:23:00,560 --> 00:23:01,760
I'm home.

366
00:23:05,700 --> 00:23:06,720
This way!

367
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:08,160
Aaaaaaah!

368
00:23:08,160 --> 00:23:09,920
Aaaaaaah!

369
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:11,380
Aaaaaaah!

370
00:23:11,380 --> 00:23:12,020
Aaaaaaah!

371
00:23:12,020 --> 00:23:12,540
Aaaaaaah!

372
00:23:12,540 --> 00:23:12,940
Aaaaaaah!

373
00:23:12,940 --> 00:23:15,240
Aaaaaaah!

374
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:15,580
Aaaaaaah!

375
00:23:15,580 --> 00:23:16,800
Aaaaaaah!

376
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:17,220
Aaaaaaah!

377
00:23:17,220 --> 00:23:18,120
Aaaaaaah!

378
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:20,300
This should be the last one,

379
00:23:20,300 --> 00:23:22,040
but I can't see Ryotsu and the others.

380
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:22,580
What?

381
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:23,700
Ryotsu!

382
00:23:25,180 --> 00:23:26,880
The money! The money!

383
00:23:27,220 --> 00:23:28,520
The money! Run!

384
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:31,580
Senpai!

385
00:23:31,840 --> 00:23:33,720
The money! The money's - !

386
00:23:34,060 --> 00:23:34,860
Let go!

387
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:36,200
Senpai!

388
00:23:36,580 --> 00:23:36,840
Whoa!

389
00:23:43,060 --> 00:23:44,360
Put it out!

390
00:23:44,520 --> 00:23:45,520
Chief!

391
00:23:45,520 --> 00:23:50,240
Our profits,
my dream of getting rich, all gone!

392
00:23:50,240 --> 00:23:51,780
Nooo!

393
00:23:53,020 --> 00:23:57,140
We'll deduct the airship damages from your pay,
you hear?

394
00:23:58,300 --> 00:23:58,780
No way.

395
00:23:59,540 --> 00:24:02,100
Why does this always happen?

396
00:24:05,700 --> 00:24:07,200
Why is that?

397
00:24:07,200 --> 00:24:08,460
Why is that?

398
00:24:08,460 --> 00:24:09,760
Why is that?

399
00:24:10,560 --> 00:24:12,880
Good work... but why?

400
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:19,380
Lemon-chan's just a kindergartener,

401
00:24:19,380 --> 00:24:22,540
so why does she love period dramas?
I wonder why.

402
00:24:22,540 --> 00:24:23,880
I wonder why.

403
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:28,600
Why is the chief's little mustache slightly small?
I wonder why.

404
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:30,020
I wonder why.

405
00:24:31,520 --> 00:24:36,560
Why does Honda's personality change when he rides a bike?
I wonder why.

406
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:37,200
So bad at it.

407
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:38,080
The kindergarten husband.

408
00:24:38,080 --> 00:24:43,380
Why does Higurashi sleep and only wake up once every four years?
I wonder why.

409
00:24:46,080 --> 00:24:52,520
Nakagawa won't lend
money to Ryo-san, though.

410
00:24:53,260 --> 00:24:56,280
They lend out tanks and
fighter jets so easily,

411
00:24:56,280 --> 00:24:59,600
I wonder why.

412
00:25:02,100 --> 00:25:06,940
Reiko-san is super rich, though,

413
00:25:08,580 --> 00:25:12,480
so why does she work at the police box?
I wonder.

414
00:25:13,380 --> 00:25:16,120
I wonder why, I wonder why.

415
00:25:16,120 --> 00:25:19,620
Why, why, why, I wonder why.

416
00:25:43,380 --> 00:25:44,818
Stay tuned! Next time,

417
00:25:44,868 --> 00:25:47,680
this is Kameari Broadcasting Station!
Nice to meet you!

418
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:50,640
That place is Kameari,

419
00:25:51,880 --> 00:25:54,180
well, surely it's Kameari,

420
00:25:55,560 --> 00:25:59,220
everyone, come on over to our town!

421
00:26:00,340 --> 00:26:00,820
Thank you!

